<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rohilla War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1773–1774</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rohilla War of 1773–1774 was a campaign in which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shuja-ud-daula">Shuja-ud-Daula</a>, Nawab of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/awadh">Awadh</a>, aided by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> troops lent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warren-hastings">Warren Hastings</a>, invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rohilkhand">Rohilkhand</a>. The Rohilla leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hafiz-rahmat-khan">Hafiz Rahmat Khan</a> was defeated and killed at Miranpur Katra in April 1774, and most of Rohilkhand was annexed to Awadh. Hastings's role was later attacked at his impeachment.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rohilla-war.jpg" alt="Rohilla War" width="320" height="249" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lord Moira · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rohilla_Horsemen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
